{"title":"Career roadmap · Research Assistant","role":"Research Assistant","summary":"A Research Assistant (RA) in psychology supports research studies by conducting literature reviews, recruiting participants, collecting and analysing data, administering research instruments, maintaining research records and helping prepare reports, presentations and publications.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Psychology"},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Strong direct alignment. Research Assistant is an appropriate entry-level target after a psychology degree, although research-intensive roles may prefer or require a master's degree."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A BA Psychology provides a strong foundation in psychological theory, research methodology, statistics and human behaviour. For long-term research careers, postgraduate study and eventually a PhD are usually important."}]},{"heading":"Typical route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BA Psychology","Research Internship/Project Assistant","Research Assistant","Research Associate","Research Coordinator / Project Manager","Research Scientist / Principal Investigator"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build research methodology, statistics, psychological assessment and academic-writing skills."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Complete postgraduate study and specialise in a research domain."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Lead studies, manage datasets/projects and contribute to publications."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward Research Scientist, Principal Investigator, academic or behavioural-science leadership roles."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When",